# vLLM v0.26.0 patch 06/18 (apply after the four DeepSeek-V4 patches above it).
#
# DeepSeek-V4 on ROCm: sparse decode and deterministic top-k by default under BI.
#
# VLLM_DS4_DECODE_KERNEL gains "auto" (the new default): sparse decode when
# VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1, the paged kernel otherwise. The deterministic top-k
# now depends only on VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT. BI=0 behaviour is unchanged.
#
# Why BI needs it: VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1 alone otherwise left decode on the
# batch-dependent paged kernel and prefill top-k on the non-deterministic one.
#
# Upstream: not yet proposed (same DeepSeek-V4 ROCm RFC as patch 02).
#
# Source commits:
#   [ROCm][DSv4][BI] Sparse decode and deterministic top-k by default under BI
#
